+# T25 — Refinement batch returns
+
+This is the execution ledger under the accepted authorial minute and `docs/PRE-MANUSCRIPT-REFINEMENT-PROTOCOL.md`. A batch return records actual read scope, change, preservation and validation. It does not confer authorial ratification. R1–R6 remain the dependency-ordered tickets in the existing map; T26 is Frank’s gate before manuscript prose.
+
+## R1.1 — Plan first and owning grounding
+
+**Standing:** substantive R1 work; R1 remains in progress. This batch does not claim the complete 144-record, whole-register or 48-movement review. The seven S bodies are not yet materialised. Their authorised subjects and homes are now governed by the amended plan.
+
+**Starting state:** actual main was `53202810778122a37973868d873335b82d8d36ca`; R1 was claimed in `f92c584aff794c017b321bf71072042233dea970`. The exact working source is `3ec712bab82dae6c9badab68c9dc4a1e66a1889c`, tree `baccd05119277cf05764fb365a8c06c4dafaff43`, after adding the execution-validation workflow. The downloaded tree was independently recreated with git and matched that tree hash. No reset of remote main was performed.
+
+### Recovered before change
+
+AGENTS, the complete current WRITING-PROTOCOL including the September 10 addendum, the refinement protocol, authorial minute, both retained input documents, central plan and orienting principles were read. The complete native core-theorems text (all eleven sections, including both Spandas, the eight determinations and crossed-zero recognition) and complete A/C body were recovered. A26/A26′/C41 and their knower/means/idealism neighbours A01/A01′, A34/A34′, C01, C10, C15, C16 and C60 were read in their actual bodies. The core theorem source house and Binary Explication source house identify the deeper support; remaining full support and register-body recovery continues within R1/R3 and is not certified by this batch.
+
+The native effects command ran successfully using exact paths for C41, A/C, A26, the core theorem source house, C10, C60, A34, A34′ and A26′. Bare `C41` failed to resolve; that invocation error is recorded rather than counted as a successful effects result. The three returned transverse paths—Mono–Poly/Two Ones, Trust/Faith/Formal Limit and Zero/Subject/Integral Logic—were read whole. The tool’s current canonical-type filter and reliance on resolved written edges mean its empty C41 consumer list is not a finding of semantic isolation.
+
+### Actual change and preserved operations
+
+The central plan was amended first. Its current §5 has exactly six product-led movements, M37–M42: Central, Actuation, AIKit, Software Factory, Workcell and Quaternal Logic. Each has its whole paired-MEF burden. S carries entrance/return, not a seventh product. The plan contains the accepted knower–means–known–whole relation and a product-specific development, rather than a new external checklist. §4’s MEF release prepares the six pairs. The immediate complete writing scope is standalone §5 after T26, without requiring seven other finished prose sections.
+
+The old §5’s mathematical meaning, triad, apoha/selection, J-space, preferences and gauges, hidden trust/labour and Poseidon’s surety, dynamic world-field, designed atlas and all E1–E6 operations remain in the plan’s substantive body. A disposition table gives their primary homes and returns. Model-as-such material lands primarily in Actuation. The former unverified novelty claim is withheld from assertion; the hard-argmax derivative is stated precisely, without claiming that discrete decisions make learning impossible.
+
+The plan’s earlier open register permutation is reconciled with its already ratified straight Vāk layering. The contradictory Offered idealism default is replaced by the existing Argued order of dependence. The raw local sixfold replaces the earlier universal six-heading gloss. Dated T20–T24 dispatch instructions are identified as historical rather than reopened. Orientation is propagated from the amended plan.
+
